#: ../decisions/0011-decide-whether-to-replace-biome-with-xo.md:1
msgid "Decide whether to replace Biome with xo"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0011-decide-whether-to-replace-biome-with-xo.md:3
msgid "Status: proposed"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0011-decide-whether-to-replace-biome-with-xo.md:4
msgid "Date: 2026-09-13"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0011-decide-whether-to-replace-biome-with-xo.md:5
msgid "Decision-makers: tkoyama010"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0011-decide-whether-to-replace-biome-with-xo.md:7
msgid "Context and Problem Statement"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0011-decide-whether-to-replace-biome-with-xo.md:9
msgid "The repository currently uses [Biome](https://biomejs.dev/) (`biome.json`, `@biomejs/biome` in `package.json`) to lint and format all TypeScript, JavaScript, JSON, and Markdown files. Biome is a single Rust binary invoked through `npm run lint` / `npm run format` and wired into pre-commit.ci. A community discussion raised [xo](https://github.com/xojs/xo) — an ESLint-based zero-config linter with the Prettier-backed `xo --fix` formatter — as a possible alternative. Should we migrate the JavaScript/TypeScript toolchain from Biome to xo, or stay on Biome?"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0011-decide-whether-to-replace-biome-with-xo.md:11
msgid "Decision Drivers"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0011-decide-whether-to-replace-biome-with-xo.md:13
msgid "**Zero-config experience**: Both tools advertise themselves as configuration-free. Any migration must not increase the amount of lint configuration the project maintains."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0011-decide-whether-to-replace-biome-with-xo.md:14
msgid "**TypeScript support**: The hand-written glue layer lives in `ts/` (including a large ambient declaration file, `ts/vtk.d.ts`). The tool must lint modern TypeScript well, including ambient declarations."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0011-decide-whether-to-replace-biome-with-xo.md:15
msgid "**Speed**: CI runs the full test suite on every PR; lint steps should stay fast."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0011-decide-whether-to-replace-biome-with-xo.md:16
msgid "**Ecosystem and rule coverage**: The project relies on the linter to catch correctness issues (unused variables, unsafe assertions, a11y for renderer code) rather than to enforce opinionated style."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0011-decide-whether-to-replace-biome-with-xo.md:17
msgid "**Maintenance overhead**: pyvista-wasm is a small project. Additional dependencies, plugins, or config drift are a real cost."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0011-decide-whether-to-replace-biome-with-xo.md:19
msgid "Considered Options"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0011-decide-whether-to-replace-biome-with-xo.md:21
msgid "**Option A: Stay on Biome (status quo)**"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0011-decide-whether-to-replace-biome-with-xo.md:22
msgid "**Option B: Migrate to xo**"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0011-decide-whether-to-replace-biome-with-xo.md:24
msgid "Decision Outcome"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0011-decide-whether-to-replace-biome-with-xo.md:26
msgid "Chosen option: \"**Option A: Stay on Biome (status quo)**\", because Biome already satisfies every decision driver while xo regresses on TypeScript depth, speed, and configuration effort for this repository."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0011-decide-whether-to-replace-biome-with-xo.md:28
msgid "TypeScript support: Biome's first-class TS parser handles `ts/vtk.d.ts` natively. xo is ESLint underneath; deep TS checking requires `@typescript-eslint` with type-aware rules, which adds setup and is slow."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0011-decide-whether-to-replace-biome-with-xo.md:29
msgid "Speed: Biome is a single Rust binary and finishes in well under a second on this repo. xo/Prettier runs the Node-based ESLint pipeline, measurably slower in CI on every PR."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0011-decide-whether-to-replace-biome-with-xo.md:30
msgid "Configuration: The project already carries `biome.json` with per-file overrides for `ts/renderer.ts` and `ts/vtk.d.ts`. Migrating means re-expressing those overrides as ESLint configuration plus a Prettier config to match the current formatting (2-space indent, width 80, semicolons) — net more configuration, not less."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0011-decide-whether-to-replace-biome-with-xo.md:31
msgid "Dependencies: Biome replaces ESLint + Prettier in one package. xo bundles ESLint, plugins, and Prettier, but the project would keep `eslint-plugin-jsdoc` as a separate dev dependency to preserve JSDoc linting, and would add Prettier's ecosystem on top."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0011-decide-whether-to-replace-biome-with-xo.md:32
msgid "Formatting parity: Biome both lints and formats with one tool and one config. xo delegates formatting to Prettier, splitting the pipeline in two for no gain here."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0011-decide-whether-to-replace-biome-with-xo.md:34
msgid "xo remains a good default for greenfield JavaScript-only projects that want the ESLint plugin ecosystem. This repository is not that: it is TypeScript-heavy, already formatted by Biome, and does not need ESLint-only plugins."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0011-decide-whether-to-replace-biome-with-xo.md:36
msgid "Consequences"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0011-decide-whether-to-replace-biome-with-xo.md:38
msgid "Good, because no migration work is needed and CI keeps its current fast lint step."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0011-decide-whether-to-replace-biome-with-xo.md:39
msgid "Good, because formatting stays stable — no repo-wide reformat diff that would pollute `git blame`."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0011-decide-whether-to-replace-biome-with-xo.md:40
msgid "Bad, because Biome's rule catalogue is smaller than ESLint's; if a future need requires an ESLint-only plugin, this decision should be revisited."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0011-decide-whether-to-replace-biome-with-xo.md:42
msgid "Confirmation"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0011-decide-whether-to-replace-biome-with-xo.md:44
msgid "Compliance is verified by the existing CI: `npm run lint` / `npm run format` (Biome) run through pre-commit.ci and GitHub Actions on every PR. If `biome.json` or `@biomejs/biome` is removed from the repository without a superseding ADR, this decision is violated."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0011-decide-whether-to-replace-biome-with-xo.md:46
msgid "Pros and Cons of the Options"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0011-decide-whether-to-replace-biome-with-xo.md:48
msgid "Option A: Stay on Biome (status quo)"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0011-decide-whether-to-replace-biome-with-xo.md:50
msgid "[Biome](https://biomejs.dev/) — single Rust toolchain for linting and formatting."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0011-decide-whether-to-replace-biome-with-xo.md:52
msgid "Good, because it is already installed, configured, and passing in CI."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0011-decide-whether-to-replace-biome-with-xo.md:53
msgid "Good, because first-class TypeScript parsing covers `ts/*.ts` and ambient declarations without extra plugins."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0011-decide-whether-to-replace-biome-with-xo.md:54
msgid "Good, because lint + format come from one binary and one config file."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0011-decide-whether-to-replace-biome-with-xo.md:55
msgid "Bad, because the plugin ecosystem is smaller than ESLint's; niche rules may not exist."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0011-decide-whether-to-replace-biome-with-xo.md:57
msgid "Option B: Migrate to xo"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0011-decide-whether-to-replace-biome-with-xo.md:59
msgid "[xo](https://github.com/xojs/xo) — opinionated ESLint wrapper with Prettier formatting."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0011-decide-whether-to-replace-biome-with-xo.md:61
msgid "Good, because it exposes the full ESLint plugin ecosystem (including `eslint-plugin-jsdoc` natively)."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0011-decide-whether-to-replace-biome-with-xo.md:62
msgid "Good, because its presets are well known in the JS community and it supports `--fix` autofix workflows."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0011-decide-whether-to-replace-biome-with-xo.md:63
msgid "Neutral, because the project does not currently use any ESLint-only plugin beyond JSDoc, which is already installed alongside Biome."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0011-decide-whether-to-replace-biome-with-xo.md:64
msgid "Bad, because TypeScript type-aware linting requires extra `@typescript-eslint` setup and is slow."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0011-decide-whether-to-replace-biome-with-xo.md:65
msgid "Bad, because formatting moves to Prettier, adding a second tool and config to keep style identical to today's Biome output."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0011-decide-whether-to-replace-biome-with-xo.md:66
msgid "Bad, because migration cost (config rewrite, repo-wide reformat, CI churn) buys no capability the project needs today."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0011-decide-whether-to-replace-biome-with-xo.md:68
msgid "More Information"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0011-decide-whether-to-replace-biome-with-xo.md:70
msgid "Current Biome configuration: [`biome.json`](../../biome.json)"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0011-decide-whether-to-replace-biome-with-xo.md:71
msgid "Lint/format entry points: `lint` and `format` scripts in [`package.json`](../../package.json)"
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0011-decide-whether-to-replace-biome-with-xo.md:72
msgid "Biome is referenced as the code-style badge in [`CONTRIBUTING.md`](../../CONTRIBUTING.md); if this decision is ever revisited, that badge and the pre-commit configuration must change together."
msgstr ""

#: ../decisions/0011-decide-whether-to-replace-biome-with-xo.md:73
msgid "Revisit triggers: a need for an ESLint-only rule or plugin, or a Biome breaking change that removes a rule the project relies on."
msgstr ""
